@page "/process"

<Seo Title="How we work" Description="Our five-step process: brief, design, build, test, launch — with weekly demos and a live client portal." />

<section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
        <h1>How we work</h1>
        <p class="lede">Clear steps, weekly demos and a live portal. You always know what's happening and what it costs.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container"><ProcessSteps /></div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
        <h2>New projects</h2>
        <p>We start with a call and a written proposal that splits the work into phases, each with its own price. Nothing is built before you approve the design. During the build you get a demo every week and can comment directly in your client portal.</p>

        <h2>Bug fixes and rescues</h2>
        <p>Send us the link, the error and, if you have it, access to the code. We reproduce the problem, find the root cause and fix it with an automated test so it can't quietly come back. You get a short written report of what was wrong and what we changed.</p>

        <h2>Upgrades</h2>
        <p>Outdated frameworks stop receiving security patches. We upgrade step by step behind automated tests — for example from .NET Framework to .NET 10 — and plan the cut-over so your users don't notice.</p>

        <h2>Payment and ownership</h2>
        <p>Invoices appear in your portal and can be paid securely by card. You own the source code, documentation and accounts from day one.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="cta-band glass">
            <h2>Ready when you are.</h2>
            <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a quote</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
